# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment Variables — copy to .env and fill in
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This project uses Turso (libsql) exclusively — no local SQLite.
# Create a free database at https://turso.tech
#
# For Vercel deployment: set both env vars in the Vercel project settings
# (https://vercel.com/dashboard → Project → Settings → Environment Variables).
# For local dev: set both in .env (copy from .env.example).

TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-db.turso.io
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# ── AI Assistant (Z.ai GLM models) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Inside the Z.ai coding sandbox the AI assistant works out of the box — no
# configuration needed. On ANY other deployment (Vercel, Netlify, Docker, your
# own domain) set ZAI_API_KEY and the app calls the public Z.ai API
# server-to-server, which works from every domain/origin (no CORS involved).
#
#   1. Create an API key: https://z.ai/manage-apikey/apikey-list
#   2. Set it here (or in your host's env-var settings) and restart:
ZAI_API_KEY=
#   3. Optional overrides:
# ZAI_MODEL=glm-4.6                     # glm-4.6 (default) | glm-4.5 | glm-4-flash
# ZAI_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4   # any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
#                                           (e.g. https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4
#                                            for Zhipu bigmodel accounts)
#
# NOTE: ZAI_CONFIG (the sandbox's internal gateway JSON) only works from
# inside the Z.ai sandbox — internal-api.z.ai resolves to private IPs and is
# unreachable from the public internet. Don't use it for real deployments;
# use ZAI_API_KEY.

# Local SQLite (development):
DATABASE_URL=file:./db/custom.db

# ── NextAuth.js (for user authentication — not yet wired up) ──────────────────
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET=  # generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Sentry error tracking (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# SENTRY_DSN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI Provider Configuration (optional — Z.ai is built in inside the sandbox)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The AI Assistant panel in the UI lets users switch providers at runtime.
# These env vars set the SERVER-SIDE DEFAULT; the user's dropdown choice
# overrides per-request.
#
#   AI_PROVIDER=zai | openai | anthropic   (default: zai)
#
# Z.ai (GLM-4.6) — built into the Z.ai sandbox (no key needed there).
# On other deployments set ZAI_API_KEY (see the "AI Assistant" section above).
#
# OpenAI — set OPENAI_API_KEY to enable in the dropdown.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o            # optional, default gpt-4o
#
# Anthropic Claude — set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY to enable in the dropdown.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022   # optional, default shown
# AI_PROVIDER=zai

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel deployment notes
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Set these env vars in Vercel:
#      TURSO_DATABASE_URL  (from Turso dashboard)
#      TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN    (from Turso dashboard)
# 2. Build command:  bun run build   (Vercel auto-detects Bun)
# 3. Install command: bun install --frozen-lockfile
# 4. Migrations run automatically on first DB connection — the app calls
#    drizzle's migrate() on startup, which applies any pending migration
#    files from ./drizzle/. No manual `drizzle-kit push` needed on Vercel.
# 5. For local dev: set TURSO_* vars in .env (same as production).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database schema migrations
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The schema is defined in src/lib/schema.ts (single source of truth).
# Migration files live in ./drizzle/ and are generated by drizzle-kit.
#
# Workflow for schema changes:
#   1. Edit src/lib/schema.ts (add/modify tables/columns)
#   2. Generate a new migration:  bun run db:generate
#   3. Commit the new file in ./drizzle/ (e.g., 0001_add_column.sql)
#   4. Push — the app auto-applies pending migrations on next startup
#
# Migrations are tracked in the __drizzle_migrations table, so each
# migration only runs once. This is idempotent and safe across deploys.
#
# Manual migration (if needed):  bun run db:migrate
# Push schema directly (dev only, no migration files):  bun run db:push
